      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under CIF (Cost, Insurance, and Freight), the seller is responsible for arranging the carriage of goods, declaring volumes to customs, delivering the goods at the named port of destination, and ensuring insurance coverage for the shipment. The seller is also responsible for collecting and paying any costs associated with tendering the goods to the carrier, including customs clearance. In the case of a shipment of electronics, the seller would typically clearly mark all necessary safety and regulatory compliance information, such as ETL or CE marks, on the packaging.",
