      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under CIF 2020, the risk of loss or damage passes from the seller to the buyer when the goods are \"placed on board the seas, inland waters, or vessels\" of the carrier, and the goods are handed over to the buyer for delivery. This is typically considered to occur when the goods are loaded onto the carrier's vessel or vehicle, marking the point of risk transfer. At this point, the seller is no longer responsible for any losses or damages occurred after the goods have been loaded onto the carrier.",
